# Node / TypeScript build artifacts for this package only.
#
# The repository root .gitignore covers `dist/` and `lib/` but not `node_modules`,
# not `out/` and not `coverage/`, so they are listed here. Kept local to the
# package for the same reason deploy/cdk-constructs/.gitignore is: the two
# concerns stay separate and a root rule cannot widen by accident.
node_modules/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test / coverage output.
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# The built extension. Root .gitignore:263 is a bare `*.vsix`, so this is already
# ignored -- it is repeated here only so someone reading this file knows the
# archive is deliberately not committed. It is a release asset built by CI, and
# unlike the committed .mcpb it cannot be drift-checked: `vsce` owns the ZIP
# writer, so the bytes are not reproducible without reimplementing it. What CI
# checks instead is the archive's member list, via `npm run verify:vsix`.
#
# The same root rule is a trap for anything else ending in .vsix. `git add` skips
# ignored files SILENTLY, so a fixture or a README named *.vsix would be written,
# verified against, and then absent from every clean checkout. That has already
# happened twice on this branch, to packaging/rpm/ash.spec (root .gitignore:102,
# a bare `*.spec`) and packaging/msix/README.msix. Nothing tracked here ends in
# .vsix: the test fixtures are ZIP archives built in memory by test/zip.ts, and
# the documentation is README.md.
*.vsix

# Nothing here should carry credentials. Listed defensively so a stray registry
# token cannot be committed by accident -- and it matters more here than in a
# library package, because publishing a VS Code extension uses a personal access
# token and that is exactly the file it would land in.
.npmrc
.vsce
